menu "Application"

config RADIO_LORAWAN
	bool "LoRaWAN radio transport"
	default y
	select LORAWAN if LORA
	help
	  App-level name for the LoRaWAN transport (issue #395) — pairs with
	  RADIO_P2P below as the two selectable radio transports. `select
	  LORAWAN if LORA` only forces the underlying Zephyr subsystem ON
	  when this is y AND the LORA radio driver is present (native_sim
	  test builds have neither — `select` on a symbol whose own
	  dependencies aren't met is a hard Kconfig error, not a silent
	  no-op, hence the `if LORA` guard); turning this off on real HW
	  (nothing else in this tree selects LORAWAN) leaves it at its own
	  default (off), disabling all radio transmission. Telemetry/alarm
	  sampling and history capture keep working with no radio
	  (app_report.c owns that cadence, not the uplink) — only the actual
	  send is skipped.

	  ~41 KB flash / ~15 KB RAM when off (issue #395) — the single
	  biggest lever of any toggle in this tree, but also the biggest
	  behavioral change (no radio at all), which is why it stays on by
	  default rather than joining debug.conf's OFF-by-default set.

config RADIO_P2P
	bool "Raw-LoRa P2P radio transport (reserved, not yet implemented)"
	default n
	help
	  Reserved app-level name for the raw-LoRa P2P transport (issue
	  #118), pairing with RADIO_LORAWAN above. The P2P implementation
	  is not merged yet — this option currently has no effect (nothing
	  depends on or selects anything from it). Wire it to the P2P
	  transport's own Kconfig once that work merges, mirroring how
	  RADIO_LORAWAN wraps CONFIG_LORAWAN.

config APP_VERBOSE_LOGGING
	bool "Enable verbose parameter logging"
	default y
	help
	  Enable verbose logging of all configuration parameters.
	  This adds detailed logging for NFC parameters and other
	  configuration changes. Disable to save flash space.

config FW_DEBUG
	bool "Debug firmware indication"
	default n
	help
	  Enable debug firmware LED indication.
	  When enabled, the periodic LED blink shows green + yellow
	  instead of just green to indicate debug build.

config APP_DEBUG_AUTOSUSPEND_S
	int "Debug auto-suspend idle timeout (seconds, 0 = disabled)"
	depends on FW_DEBUG && POWEROFF && SHELL_BACKEND_RTT
	default 7200
	help
	  On the Debug build, after this many seconds with no RTT/shell
	  activity the device enters deep-sleep (STM32 Shutdown via
	  sys_poweroff) so a forgotten bench unit stops draining its
	  battery — Debug FW runs with CONFIG_PM=n, so the CPU never sleeps
	  and the quiescent draw is high. Default 7200 s (2 h). 0 disables
	  the auto-suspend.
	  Wake is by NRST / power-cycle (clean boot; NVS identity and
	  LoRaWAN keys survive in flash).

config APP_LORAWAN_1_1
	bool "Use LoRaWAN 1.1.x crypto for OTAA"
	default n
	help
	  Enable LoRaWAN 1.1.x crypto for OTAA join: feed `lrw_nwkkey` into
	  the NwkKey slot (distinct from AppKey). When disabled (default,
	  LoRaWAN 1.0.x), the firmware copies `lrw_appkey` into both the
	  NwkKey and AppKey slots so the JoinRequest MIC is computed from
	  AppKey — required for 1.0.x network servers (TTN, ChirpStack,
	  Helium).

	  Enabling this also requires the LoRaMac library to be built with
	  USE_LRWAN_1_1_X_CRYPTO=1; the Kconfig only flips the app-level
	  key wiring.

config APP_NFC_ENCRYPTION
	bool "Encrypt the NFC command/config channel (AES-CCM)"
	default y
	help
	  Production default (y): NFC command records (hio.stck:cmd) and config
	  records (hio.stck:cfg) must be AES-CCM encrypted with the device
	  secret_key and a strictly increasing nonce, and the response written
	  back (hio.stck:rsp) is encrypted the same way. Without the key, the
	  only thing a phone can read is the plaintext info record (hio.stck:inf).

	  Disable (n) ONLY for a bench validation build, to drive the NFC command
	  and config channel in plaintext without provisioning a secret key or
	  managing nonces. Such a build logs a loud boot warning. NEVER ship a
	  build with this turned off.

config APP_CCM_HW_AES
	bool "Use the STM32WL hardware AES peripheral for NFC AES-CCM"
	depends on APP_NFC_ENCRYPTION && SOC_SERIES_STM32WLX
	default y
	help
	  Back the app_ccm (RFC 3610 AES-CCM) block cipher with the STM32WL on-die
	  AES peripheral (register-level, no HAL/Zephyr-crypto dependency). This is
	  what lets the build drop mbedTLS entirely (~6.5 KB flash, #261).

	  Disable (n) to fall back to the LoRaMac soft-SE AES (peripherals/soft-se,
	  already in flash) as the block cipher instead — the CCM layer is identical,
	  only the primitive differs. The host unit tests use this software path.

config APP_CMD_DEBUG_SHELL
	bool "Shell injector for downlink command dispatcher"
	depends on SHELL
	default n
	help
	  Enable `tester cmd <transport> <hex>` for end-to-end testing
	  of the downlink command dispatcher without a LoRaWAN gateway.
	  The hex payload is fed to app_cmd_handle as if it had arrived
	  from the given transport (lrw or nfc) and the encoded response
	  is logged and (for lrw) queued on port 85.

config APP_HISTORY_FLASH
	bool "Persist sensor history in the history_partition flash"
	default y
	help
	  Store the sensor history store-and-forward buffer in the dedicated
	  history_partition flash (NVS), surviving reboot and power loss.
	  Disable to use a __noinit RAM ring of CONFIG_APP_HISTORY_BYTES
	  instead; data is then lost on power loss.

	  Builds with this enabled must keep CONFIG_FLASH_LOAD_SIZE at the
	  history_partition offset so the linker stops the image from growing
	  into the runtime-written flash (see prj.conf); builds with it
	  disabled (debug.conf) may relax the budget up to the
	  storage_partition offset.

config APP_HISTORY_BYTES
	int "History RAM fallback ring size (bytes)"
	default 1024
	help
	  Size of the in-RAM history ring used when CONFIG_APP_HISTORY_FLASH=n.
	  Record size is variable (5-33 B) depending on the enabled sensor set.

config APP_CALIBRATION
	bool "Factory calibration mode (magnet-triggered)"
	default y
	help
	  Compile in the magnet-triggered factory calibration mode
	  (app_calibration.c): boots into a dedicated LED/LoRaWAN test loop
	  that reads every enabled sensor and reports over a fixed uplink,
	  instead of normal application behavior.

	  Disable for bench sessions that don't need to calibrate hardware
	  (e.g. a pure radio/transport test) to free flash/RAM for what IS
	  under test — see app/debug.conf's variant table.

config APP_PYQ1648
	bool "PIR motion sensor (PYQ1648)"
	default y
	help
	  Compile in the PIR motion-detector driver wrapper (app_pyq1648.c).
	  Default y to match shipped behavior — both this and
	  CONFIG_APP_BUZZER stay compiled in on a normal build, since which
	  one is actually active is a runtime, per-unit choice
	  (cap_pir_detector / cap_buzzer config, they share pins, #90/#338).
	  Disable only for a bench session that knows it needs neither.

config APP_BUZZER
	bool "Buzzer / melody output (#338)"
	default y
	help
	  Compile in the buzzer/melody driver wrapper (app_buzzer.c) and its
	  shell (`ats buzz ...`) and remote-command (NFC/LoRaWAN play-melody)
	  surfaces. Default y to match shipped behavior (see
	  CONFIG_APP_PYQ1648 above) — disable only for a bench session that
	  knows it needs neither PIR nor buzzer.

endmenu

menu "Zephyr Kernel"
source "Kconfig.zephyr"
endmenu
